\subsection{\href{https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/rcs.cite.belyi}{How to cite Belyi maps}}
\begin{definition}\label{rcs.cite.belyi}
\uses{}
\leanok
If you use the database of Belyi maps in your research please cite:

\href{https://doi.org/10.2140/obs.2019.2.375}{*A database of Belyi maps*}, by Michael Musty, Sam Schiavone, Jeroen Sijsling, and John Voight, Proceedings of the Thirteenth Algorithmic Number Theory Symposium (ANTS-XIII), eds. Renate Scheidler and Jonathan Sorenson, Open Book Series 2, Mathematical Sciences Publishers, Berkeley, 2019, 375-392 \cite{mr:3952023},

as well as any of the references cited above that are of particular relevance.
\end{definition}


